#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096417 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096617 :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function"}] :question/id #uuid "d7a77a89-0535-54da-a246-36ee5b4e9e7f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3634" :question/problem "Differentiate $x\\cos x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\cos x .$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t (x\\cos x)' &=   u'(x) \\cdot v(x) + u(x) \\cdot v'(x)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t&= (x)'\\cdot \\cos x + x\\cdot (\\cos x)'\\\n\t\t\t\t\t   & = 1 \\cdot \\cos x + x (-\\sin x)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t  & =  \\cos x - x \\sin x\t\t\t\t\t\n\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235429 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059675 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of an Expression With Sine or Cosine Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f82a959f-469c-580d-b699-744a01e1a73e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{cos}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f82a959f-469c-580d-b699-744a01e1a73e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{cos}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234938} :answer-field/id #uuid "01d3bdac-6753-510d-b7d4-b1bb408d2f9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234978}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a37e3e9-7f1b-5a8d-b564-d8b93eaac32a" :question/math-academy-id "q-167324" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We know that \n\n$$\n\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nApplying this formula and the constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :step/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235739 :step/id #uuid "c2c98eb5-4423-57c5-b4bb-0778bf19de27"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514433 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059675 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of an Expression With Sine or Cosine Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f06a75e2-cb48-5e18-9b9c-3baddcbbb99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f06a75e2-cb48-5e18-9b9c-3baddcbbb99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\cos x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514159} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c175b32-cf9f-563c-b23b-dd0064f3ca32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83dc5138-e470-5b8f-b97c-b3006ebeb428" :question/math-academy-id "q-166071" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}\\,=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We know that \n\n$$\n\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nApplying this formula and the constant multiple rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :step/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514509 :step/id #uuid "710f4f2b-0d09-5252-85a4-0e43efb200b1"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096619 :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent Line to a Product  at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2f634bf-1fab-5c5c-9faf-cca696e95edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514126}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2f634bf-1fab-5c5c-9faf-cca696e95edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514126} :answer-field/id #uuid "f49d4659-1c96-5a65-a285-84ed00e2cd31" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d1eaed8d-b238-536c-b3a6-a6e7f9e94a12" :question/math-academy-id "q-166073" :question/problem "If a curve $C$ is defined by the equation $y=f(x)\\cdot h(x),$ calculate the slope of the tangent line to the curve at the point where $x=\\pi .$\n\nSlope $\\,=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate using the product rule. Recall that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}$ and $h(x)=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x})=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =f\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x}+h\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of the tangent line, we now substitute $x=\\pi $ into the formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\pi } & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{\\pi }(-1+0) \\\\  & =2{e}^{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line is $2{e}^{\\pi }.$" :step/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514493 :step/id #uuid "20a1a95d-5d23-50cc-a5eb-c111e96d8376"}]}]}
